    "body": "Great catch! This fixes the ANSI escape code width calculation issue in `starship explain`.\n\nThe fix works correctly, but I noticed a performance impact - `width_graphemes()` now compiles the regex on every call. Consider using `std::sync::OnceLock` to cache the compiled regex:\n\n```rust\nuse std::sync::OnceLock;\n\nstatic ANSI_REGEX: OnceLock<Regex> = OnceLock::new();\n\nfn get_ansi_regex() -> &'static Regex {\n    ANSI_REGEX.get_or_init(|| Regex::new(r\"\\x1B\\[[0-9;]*m\").unwrap())\n}\n\n// Then in width_graphemes():\nfn width_graphemes(&self) -> usize {\n    get_ansi_regex()\n        .replace_all(self.as_ref(), \"\")\n        .graphemes(true)\n        .map(Grapheme)\n        .map(|g| g.width())\n        .sum()\n}\n```\n\nOtherwise LGTM! 👍",
